The legal texts come from official publications of the Estado Plurinacional de Bolivia:

  Fuente: Gaceta Oficial del Estado Plurinacional de Bolivia (texto de consulta),
  http://www.gacetaoficialdebolivia.gob.bo/app/webroot/archivos/CONSTITUCION.pdf
  (read through the Internet Archive capture of 6 October 2026), retrieved 28 October 2026;
  the preamble from the Tribunal Constitucional Plurinacional's edition,
  https://tcpbolivia.bo/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/CPE_2009.pdf, retrieved 28 October 2026.

The Gaceta marks its text "TEXTO DE CONSULTA" and "Derechos Reservados © Gaceta Oficial de Bolivia", and no
source publishes a licence. They are official legal texts; their copyright status is not confirmed here, and they
are reproduced with the attribution above.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes, dashes and ligature glyphs were normalised; page numbers and running headers were removed; headings
were gathered in one structure file; and the text was arranged as git commits credited to the norms and rulings
concerned. The wording of the law was not changed. None of the publishers endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
